url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab21/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyuns is a browser-based, noncommercial toy that follows only the
  broad frame of Strikers 1945 II (Psikyo, arcade, 1997): a vertically
  scrolling shooter on a tall 240x320 field with a shot, a three-level
  charge shot released by letting go of a held key, and a bomb, each
  different for the four aircraft (XF5U Flying Pancake, Ki-84 Hayate,
  P-38 Lightning, J7W Shinden); seven stages, each with a mid-boss and a boss; and three
  difficulty levels (beginner, intermediate, advanced). The number of lives
  (1-9), the number of bombs (0-5), the starting stage (1-7) and the paper
  colour (rough cream or sketchbook white) are chosen through a program
  written in the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang. Input is
  keyboard, touch and gamepad, with fullscreen; the game is saved in three
  browser slots and can be exported to and imported from a .dhsave file
  that includes every enemy, bullet and the random-number state. The one
  image file is the title on the start screen, written by hand by the
  author's wife; every aircraft, enemy, boss, terrain and the paper grain
  is drawn by code as wobbly graphite strokes when the page opens, in
  greyscale on paper. Defeating the final boss is celebrated with falling
  petals and a short fanfare synthesised in the browser from the trio melody
  of Elgar's Pomp and Circumstance March No. 1 (1901, public domain); no
  recording is used. No graphics, sound, text, stage layout, bullet data
  or code of the original game is used or extracted; all numbers are the
  author's own. The MIT license applies to the Donghyuns code and
  documentation; the page fonts are under the SIL Open Font License, and
  the handwritten title remains the work of its writer. See
  LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
